## §C CONSTRAINTS

- Jekyll + minima theme. Ruby/bundler, ⊥ npm.
- local preview = `jekyll@<NAME>.service` → `serve-local.sh` → `bundle exec jekyll serve --baseurl /<NAME>` on port `<PORT>`. ⊥ `jekyll serve` by hand.
- deps in `Gemfile.local`, ⊥ a file named `Gemfile` — GitHub Pages builds against a literal `Gemfile` w/ its own gem set. bundler installs to project-local `vendor/bundle` (`.bundle/config`).
- reverse-proxied at `/<NAME>/`, `stripPrefix: false` ∴ the `/<NAME>` baseurl is required.
- `README.md` IS the site index (`permalink: /`). ⊥ an `index.html`.

## §I INTERFACES

- url: `GET /<NAME>/` → the site, through claude-hub
- card: `README.md` H1 → title, ¶1 → description, frontmatter `tags: [...]` → badges
- file: `_config.yml` — `title`, `description`, `theme`, `exclude`

## §V INVARIANTS

- V1: served `baseurl` = `/<NAME>` = sentinel `proxyPrefix`. any ≠ → every link & asset breaks under the proxy.
- V2: preview deps ∈ `Gemfile.local`. ⊥ create `Gemfile` — Pages would build against it & the two configs fight.
- V3: `.project-meta.json` `routes` ! track the permalink scheme. change `permalink:`/add a collection → update `routes`, else Browse's eye-icon previews 404.
- V4: `README.md` H1/¶1/`tags` = the landing card's title/description/badges. ⊥ let them drift from §G.
- V5: agent-facing files (`AGENTS.md`, `SPEC.md`, `.project-meta.json`, `serve-local.sh`, `Gemfile.local*`, `vendor`) ∈ `_config.yml` `exclude`. ⊥ ship them in the built site.

